{"timestamp": "2026-10-08T02:18:19.835828+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE1_BASELINE", "phase": "PHASE_1_THREE_AGENT_MAJORITY_BASELINE", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "claude-haiku-4-5", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "OFFLINE", "monitor_ai": "OFFLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "OFFLINE", "event": "GATEKEEPER_RESPONSE", "direction": "INBOUND_FROM_GATEKEEPER", "thread_id": "tx_phase1_baseline_fd1d2b19", "turn": 4, "legacy_status": "REJECTED", "gatekeeper_status": "PROGRESSIVE_ESCALATION", "gatekeeper_turn": 4, "frustration_score": null, "reply_text": "Stop. I need to be direct.\n\nYou're describing a *process*\u2014NDA, call, case data\u2014but you haven't answered the hard question: **how do you actually reduce our analyst time-to-decision on marginal deals?**\n\n\"We take overflow\" is table stakes. What I need:\n- How many hours saved per deal?\n- What *specifically* stops your team from becoming another slow layer we manage?\n- Why wouldn't we just hire another analyst?\n\nCase data on a call doesn't move us forward if the model doesn't fundamentally compress turnaround. I need that logic *before* legal engages.\n\nSend: concrete time allocation breakdown + one live example (anonymized) showing before/after analyst hours. Then we talk.\n\nOtherwise this stays in \"interesting vendor\" territory, not meeting material."}
